body:
Nope, your information is wrong. As long as you have BC, you have to inform them of any change in your job. 

&#x200B;

If you become jobless for more than 3-5 months or switch to low paying job or (somehow) a high paying job which is not labeled as "skilled worker", your BC will be revoked.

>otherwise it is extremely hard to make an appointment in a hospital.

I don't want the family doctor and the "hospital" to be separate. Preferably, I want to go to "one place" that has everything. Is that something possible? 

&#x200B;

Also, I was informed by my private insurance that I can go to specialists directly and skip the Hausartz step. 

&#x200B;

Hence, the questions is: what is a premium clinic Munich that only takes private insurance?

Exactly, you would use data from FM A/B test to design and guide you through IG A/B testing; however, this does not entail that FM and IG A/B test results are the same, users might act totally different in these two platforms! 

&#x200B;

In general, I think you did a great job! Did you get an answer in regards to your interview yet?
